  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions

  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Commerce is trade plus everything that helps trade happen — transport, banking, insurance, warehousing, advertising and communication. Production belongs to industry.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Quarrying is extraction — primary industry. The other three are commercial services.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Moving a good to where it is wanted creates place utility. Storage creates time utility; manufacturing creates form utility.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The Partnership Act default is equal shares, whatever the capital. A deed exists precisely to displace that default.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    There is no legal separation between the trader and the business, so his personal property is at risk.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The patronage dividend returns surplus in proportion to how much each member traded with the society — one member, one vote still governs control.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The restriction on share transfer keeps ownership within a known group. The fifty limit applies to members, not employees.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The memorandum governs the company's external relations: name, objects, liability and capital.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    A debenture is a loan, so its holder is a creditor entitled to interest whether or not profit is made.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Water, electricity and rail are network monopolies where one supplier is efficient but private monopoly is unacceptable, so the state supplies.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The company survives its members and caps their loss at their shares.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Selling to the final consumer is the retailer's function; that is what makes him a retailer.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    One owner, many branches, central buying and a common name — the multiple shop.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    It fixes the invoice price for the trade buyer and is not entered in the ledger separately.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Mark-up is profit over cost: 3,000 ÷ 12,000 = 25%. The margin would be 3,000 ÷ 15,000 = 20%.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    20,000 × 0.9 = 18,000; 18,000 × 0.95 = 17,100. Discounts in a chain are taken one after the other, never added.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    A village market sale is direct: the farmer meets the consumer with no middleman.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The visible balance counts goods only; imports larger than exports is a deficit.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Freight is a service, so it is invisible. Only goods are visible.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    A quota limits quantity; a tariff raises price and yields revenue. An embargo is the total ban.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    That triple function is why a bank will release payment against it.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The bank's promise replaces the unknown foreign buyer's promise with a known bank's.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    150 ÷ 120 × 100 = 125. Above 100 means a unit of export buys more than the base period's imports.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The goods enter the country only to leave again; Rotterdam and Singapore are classic examples.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Insurance pools risk: many pay small premiums so that the few who lose are made whole.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The crossing is a direction to the paying bank to collect through an account, which leaves a trail.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Indemnity restores without enriching; a new-for-old payment would breach it.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Bond is the customs arrangement that defers duty until the goods leave the store.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Rail carries heavy loads at low cost per tonne-km. Pipelines are cheaper still but only for fluids.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    It tells the market that the product exists and what it does — the informative job.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The depositor lends for a term, so the bank pays more than on a current account.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    It measures the short-term funds free after the short-term debts are allowed for.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    A debenture runs for years; the others fall due within a year or on demand.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The seller is the party who owes the reduction, so the seller issues the credit note.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Errors and omissions excepted: the seller may correct a clerical mistake without repudiating the sale.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    The bull buys in the expectation of selling at a higher price.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    It is collected by the seller and passed on, so the burden is on the consumer and the tax is indirect.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Ownership moves; commercialisation merely asks a state firm to behave commercially.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    Redress is the remedy — repair, replacement, refund or damages.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.12pt)[
    It goes beyond the legal minimum, which is what distinguishes it from compliance.
  ]

]

